                  <article class="doc">
                    <h4>Rounding</h4>
                    <p>
                      Money is stored in minor units: cents, pence, yen. Every amount that reaches the
                      <a>Ledger</a> is already an integer, so rounding happens before a value is written,
                      never after.
                    </p>
                    <h5>Where it happens</h5>
                    <p class="doc__changed">
                      <span class="doc__gone">Each invoice line rounds its own total.</span>
                      <span class="doc__insert"
                        ><span class="doc__typed">Rounding happens once, in the ledger, using half to even. Invoices pass exact totals and let the ledger round them, so a long invoice no longer drifts a cent per line.</span
                        ><span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cursor__flag">Claude</span></span
                        ><span class="doc__rest"></span
                      ></span>
                    </p>
                    <h5>Why half to even</h5>
                    <p>
                      Rounding half up nudges totals upward across many entries. Half to even matches
                      how existing entries were written, which <a>Reconciliation</a> depends on.
                    </p>
                  </article>
                </div>
